            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f3" n="3" xml:id="d391-f3-content">
                <p>Dated Oct. 23; see <ref target="#d390-f3">footnote 3, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >supra</hi>.</ref></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f4" n="4" xml:id="d391-f4-content">
                <p>The draft reply by Dulles to Papagos was not sent. (Text attached to memorandum
                    by O’Connor to Byroade, Nov. 2; 747C.00/11–254.) A memorandum by Phyllis D.
                    Bernau (S) of a telephone call by Eisenhower to Dulles, Nov. 3, noted that
                    Eisenhower “thought the draft was cold and abrupt.” Dulles “said he would go
                    over it more carefully.” (Eisenhower Library, Dulles papers, Telephone
                    Conversations)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
